HST Office: Office-style collapse ladder for the ribbon groups (step-by-step large, medium, small).

Owner decision (2026-11-07): the step-by-step collapse ships on; the CollapseLadder switch
(org.openoffice.Office.HSTRibbon, hst-ribbon-switches.patch) is rollback safety only.

Before any group folds into the chevron popup, the groups of a ribbon tab shrink one state at a
time, from the right: large (as authored), medium (large buttons become small icons with the label
on the right), small (icons only). Only what still does not fit folds, so the chevron is the last
rung and no group is clipped. A toolbox holding Paste keeps its authored size, as in Office; a
folded group opens in the popup at its full size. The choice is the pure, monotone ladder of
vcl/inc/HstRibbonScaling.hxx (hst-ribbon-scaling-helper.patch); widths per state are measured once
per group and content and cached, so a resize only applies the states that change.

- vcl/inc/HstRibbonLadder.hxx, vcl/source/control/HstRibbonLadder.cxx (new): group states, the switch.
- vcl/source/control/PriorityMergedHBox.cxx, vcl/inc/PriorityMergedHBox.hxx: the ladder before the fold.
- vcl/inc/toolbox.h, vcl/source/window/toolbox.cxx: the authored toolbox style and the text position
  are kept for the ladder; a later text position change relayouts the toolbox.
- vcl/Library_vcl.mk: builds HstRibbonLadder.

